## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to build a small, end-to-end, event-driven ingestion pipeline with validation, deduplication, and safe file relocation using Cloud Functions, BigQuery, and Cloud Storage. It also invites discussion on idempotency, IAM boundaries, and testability.

## Key Concepts

- Cloud Functions as event-driven processors for Storage events
- JSONL validation and per-line schema checks
- Deduplication using insertId in BigQuery streaming/bulk loads
- File lifecycle: moving processed files to an archive path
- Minimal IAM bindings and a practical test plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Sketch of a Cloud Function triggered by Storage events
exports.incomingClicks = async (event, context) => {
  const filePath = `gs://${event.bucket}/${event.name}`;
  // read file, parse lines, validate fields, batch insert to BigQuery with insertId
  // on success, move file to processed/ path
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale for very large files and avoid memory issues?
- How would you test idempotency and ensure no duplicates in BigQuery?

