- What metrics would you monitor to balance false positives vs drift detection latency?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses end-to-end real-time ingestion, deduplication guarantees, and exactly-once semantics across regional boundaries. Tests Dataflow configuration (watermarks, lateness), BigQuery writes with insertId, and robust monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow streaming and Pub/Sub in multi-region setups
- Stateful deduplication by event_id
- BigQuery insertId for idempotent sinks
- Watermarking and allowed lateness
- Cloud Monitoring alerts and incident wiring
- IAM least privilege and service accounts

## Code Example

```java
class DedupDoFn extends DoFn<Event, Event> {
  @StateId("seen") private final StateSpec<ValueState<Boolean>> seen = null;
  @ProcessElement
  public void process(@Element Event e, @StateId("seen") ValueState<Boolean> seen) {
    if (Boolean.FALSE.equals(seen.read())) {
      seen.write(true);
      out.output(e);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotence and backpressure under traffic spikes?
- What monitoring dashboards would you set up for latency and data-lag, and how would you handle alert fatigue?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design real-time, multi-tenant data pipelines with correct deduplication, rate limiting, and safe cross-tenant isolation. It also probes for practical IAM scoping, dead-letter handling, and observability under burst traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion, Apache Beam (Dataflow) processing
- Deduplication by tenant_id + event_id with windowing
- Per-tenant rate limiting using Redis
- External risk-score enrichment via internal API
- Multi-tenant BigQuery routing: analytics.tenants.{tenant}.events
- Dead-letter queues, exponential backoff retries
- Least-privilege IAM, monitoring, alerting, cost control

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam-style dedup snippet
// Deduplicate by (tenant_id, event_id) using per-tenant state
class DedupFn {
  process(element) {
    const key = element.tenant_id + ':' + element.event_id;
    if (state.has(key)) return;
    state.add(key);
    yield element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant rate limiting and data skew at scale?
- How would you secure Redis and ensure tenant isolation for secrets?
- How would you handle late-arriving events that would violate dedup windows?

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario tests comprehensive GCP data engineering skills including end-to-end data flow design, data validation, privacy compliance, and reliability patterns for beginners. It specifically evaluates understanding of idempotent writes via insertId and proper data retention practices.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Functions (event-driven processing)
- Pub/Sub (asynchronous messaging)
- Cloud Run (containerized services)
- BigQuery (data warehousing)
- Cloud Storage (object storage)
- Data validation and schema enforcement
- PII redaction and privacy protection
- Idempotent operations and deduplication
- IAM principles and least privilege
- Retry strategies and error handling

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function redactPII(event, salt) {
  if (event.user_id) {
    event.user_id = crypto.createHash('sha256')
      .update(event.user_id + salt)
      .digest('hex');
  }
  if (event.device_id) {
    event.device_id = crypto.createHash('sha256')
      .update(event.device_id + salt)
      .digest('hex');
  }
  return event;
}
```

